# Q: the city falls the way it was written to: anything, and the factory by name.
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --mission b4_berlin --probe tools/probe/b4_berlin.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/b4-berlin.txt
#
# The two objectives are two kinds of ledger: any three structures, and the factory by role.
# The probe fights it the way a player would rather than the way a script might split it:
# one fist, driven onto the factory, and the base taken apart from the inside out — a column
# on a move order engages what it meets, which is how buildings the script did not name fall
# to a script that stays short. Slots are the force as it actually stands: the formations
# leave gaps in the numbering, and an order to a gap is an order to the dead.

objectives
teams

# Positions read off `structures 2` for this seed; slots read off `units soviet`.
# The orders go first: four hundred ticks of somebody else's war is four hundred
# ticks in which slots die before the script can reach them.
structures 2
